      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A guide can cover several themes, and the group can express preferences before the visit starts.\", \"decision\": \"How should a short guided visit choose its emphasis?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe guide proposes a short visit with one theme and adjusts it after hearing preferences. A prepared route provides a starting point for changes.\nThe guide offers two themes for the short visit and lets the group choose between them. The group makes a clear collective choice within a limited set.\nThe guide gathers theme preferences and builds the short visit around the most shared interest. The route reflects the particular group."
    }
